WEBVTT

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.190
Salmon                                                         Vegetables                    Hamburg Steak

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.190
Food! Food!

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.730
Yumoto, this is already your third meal of the day.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.600
I just get so hungry after a cuddle!

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.570
Hey, I'll take this!

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.520
Being young is an amazing thing.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.500
In his case, I don't think it has
anything to do with being young.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.590
In my case,

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:29.640
eating without a tablecloth on the table
always cuts my appetite in half, but...

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.470
President, Vice President, 
what about you two?

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.490
I've heard that in Europe during the Middle Ages,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.430
they used the tablecloth to wipe their mouths.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.440
I'm grateful that they changed 
that to individual napkins.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.140
Speaking of which,

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.890
it's a shame the cafeteria has 
no finger bowls, don't you think?

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.110
Oh, that's true.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.490
Let's see if we can find room 
for it in the Student Council funds.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.150
Box lunch! Box lunch! It makes me so happy!

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.660
Box lunch! Box lunch! Steamy hot!

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.130
You gotta eat it while it's still warm!

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.010
The existence of such base and vulgar 
individuals here at Binan High School

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.880
absolutely cannot be permitted.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.020
In other words, you want to do something about

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.330
the members of that Earth Defense Club thing?

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.970
You catch on quickly, Akoya.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:52.900
Love is Something You Wear on Your Back

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.360
<b>Earth Defense Club (lol)</b>

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.100
Oh, my...

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.900
An afternoon cuddle after lunch 
makes me feel so much better!

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.320
Everyone!

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.830
Don't you think it's strange?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.810
<b>Potato Chips</b>

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.440
What is?

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.250
That we pretend we don't see the cuddling?

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.850
No! I mean the monsters!

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.500
Oh? Did another one show up?

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.040
Not that!

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.050
Don't you think it's strange?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.190
They always seem to appear close to us.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.190
Now that you mention it...

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.610
You think the enemy could 
be closer than we thought?

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:30.060
It's true, they do appear awfully 
frequently within our area of activity.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:33.060
Yeah, they seem to show up just 
as we start talking about them.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.900
Pardon me, Defense Club members.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.230
What is that stench?

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.200
Hey, Gero-kun. Can we help you?

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.310
The truth is, I came to inform you

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.270
that while your group has been approved as a club,

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:02.010
student council rule 132 states that

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.050
if the club members' final exam 
scores do not meet the average,

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.310
your club will be dissolved.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.780
Huh? There's a rule like that?

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.760
It was just established.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.070
Well, that's all I wanted to say.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:18.850
That stench...

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.990
Is there a dead animal here?

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.370
You've got the right idea.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.290
I-Is that all you wanted?

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.730
Yes. I'll be going, then.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.750
What are you looking at?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.360
Weren't you the one looking at me?

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:45.110
Doesn't that guy have the 
wrong idea about something?

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.360
Maybe he's interested in you, Ryuu?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.100
Cut that out. It's gross.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.750
What is this unpleasant sensation?

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:57.460
Really, I wish that club would just fall apart.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.980
I cannot allow it!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.030
The Earth Defense Club, 
so full of love, must not be dissolved!

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:09.150
But from their perspective, 
we must seem pretty incomprehensible.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.690
Well, that's true.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.800
Even so, we must prevent 
the club's dissolution!

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.500
You're so passionate! 
Have your needs been building up?

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.050
That's <i>you</i>.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.490
Silence!

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.450
Listen, all of you!

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:25.250
You absolutely must see to it that 
your test scores beat the average!

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.510
That is an order!

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:37.660
Ryuu, do you think 
you'll do okay on the finals?

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.190
Nah, probably not.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.760
You've got it good, Kinugawa-senpai.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.110
You always get top scores.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.780
Well, I suppose.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.660
But I can't get 100s like En-chan does.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.890
Yufuin-senpai, you've 
gotten perfect scores before?

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.540
Yeah, when I successfully 
guess the subject matter.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.020
So if there's no need to worry about Io...

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.220
I guess the real problem is Yumoto.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.630
Yumoto's an unknown quantity, huh?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.640
An unknown quantity?

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.980
I hear that in math, he can tell the 
area of a shape just by looking at it.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.530
Without any calculations?

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.160
No calculation at all.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.650
He probably doesn't know 
the equations, after all.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.340
Wow.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.450
But since his way of thinking is so unique,

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:20.100
in subjects like Japanese, he can easily get zeroes.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.110
So, how's the bath?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.360
Yumoto, are you going to do okay on your tests?

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.570
I'm not motivated at all.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.040
Hey, hey.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.490
After all, I'm inheriting the 
family bath, so I don't need school!

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:39.250
Yumoto. You must not become a man like me.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.460
A man good for nothing but chopping wood...

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.940
Big bro...

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.790
Now, now. It's because
your brother chops the wood

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.930
that we can enjoy the baths, after all.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.890
But isn't Kurotama Bath's selling point 
that it runs off a free-flowing hot spring?

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.180
So it shouldn't really need firewood, right?

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:01.660
Then what does he chop wood for?

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.200
Why do you, big bro?

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:10.110
I think the screws in my 
brother's head might be loose.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.580
You're one to talk.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.530
Hey. Speaking of screws, do you 
know why they're called "screws"?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.510
Because you screw them in?

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.340
Oh, I see!

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.970
They're screws because you screw them in.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.970
You mean that wasn't a quiz, 
just a normal question?

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.790
That's amazing!

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.050
Ryuu-senpai, you're amazing!

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.780
The riddle I've been puzzling over 
since third grade is solved!

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.860
Yay! Yay! I did it!

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.860
That's too long to puzzle over something! Look it up!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:45.500
Naruko-senpai gets good grades 
and he's rich. He's amazing.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.830
He pretty much has no faults at all!

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.410
H-Hey.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.890
My name is Itsumo Ichiban.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:03.480
<b>Itsumo Ichiban</b>

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:03.130
As my name implies, my grades are "always #1."

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:08.050
But people still find me creepy because they say I sound dumb when I talk.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.400
I don't particularly care, though.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.000
You know, Itsumo-senpai gets good grades,

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.900
but isn't the way he talks kinda odd?

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.240
I think he's got just one screw loose.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.030
What do you mean, "kinda odd"?

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:21.620
If you think I'm creepy, just say I'm creepy.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:24.810
And why would you say "just one screw"?

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.740
Why be so specific about that?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.690
He talks to himself an awful lot.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.690
Gets under my skin...

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.270
Oh, is that the time? I've got to hurry.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.150
Oh, pardon me.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.040
I've been wondering...

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:45.750
Why does a man of your caliber 
associate with that bunch?

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.960
Are you talking to me?

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.070
Of course.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:54.110
Someone like you would fit 
right in with the student council.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.180
Is there any profit in listening to this?

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:05.150
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:06.940
And so, I think the student council 
requires a head accountant

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.890
who's an expert in modern finance.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:12.240
In other words, a treasurer.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.610
It's true that we're dealing 
with large sums of money here.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.090
So, do you have any candidates?

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:21.120
They must have both the
intelligence and refinement

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.580
suitable to our student council.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.540
Yes, I have one.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.250
Me? Become the student council's treasurer?

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.310
I don't think it's a bad deal at all.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:39.140
Of course, we know you're 
involved in the Defense Club, too.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.150
We don't expect you to answer right away.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:43.140
No, I'll join.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.570
If it will make me a profit.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:51.140
To ask for money in exchange for a 
position on the sacred student council...

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.480
But that's interesting.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.950
Then we will pay you adequate compensation.

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:03.530
I'm always #1 in my grade, 
so why is it #2 Naruko instead of me?

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.920
I can't understand it...

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:09.080
<i>Now, even if they manage
to clear the test hurdle,</i>

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.270
<i>the Defense Club will be
left with four members.</i>

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:18.930
<b>Wombat
Born November 30th
 (converted to Earth calendar)
Blood Type A (probably) / Sagittarius
Hobby: World peace
Likes: Love, spinach</b>

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.240
Okay, start your tests.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:25.040
Okay! Let's do this!

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.710
Didn't you say you were tired before?

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:31.530
I am tired, but I won't sleep well if 
the club is dissolved because of me.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.440
It gets under my skin so bad...

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.330
He's the one person I can't lose to.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:43.360
Of course, I'm going to be #1 like always...

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:44.970
Itsumo, something wrong?

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.180
<b>Combined Finals Rankings</b>

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.240
Hey, what are you doing?

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:56.900
No pushing! What's with you?

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.340
Score

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.340
Wh-What is this?!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:04.600
Th-This must not happen!

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.510
H-He makes money and gets #1,

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:10.160
while I do nothing but study and get #2...

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.450
It's unforgivable!

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.990
Are you all right, Lord Zundar?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.500
There.

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:26.920
He will be our target this time!

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.760
<b>Earth Defense Club                           (lol)</b>

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.680
Oh, wow!

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.760
I got another zero in Japanese!

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.630
That's okay, it was within expectations.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.760
How'd you do, Zaou-san?

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.710
To be frank, I didn't reach average in anything.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.640
It's okay.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:44.100
Naruko's high grades mean our
second year guys averaged out.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.490
Thank you, Io!

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:49.080
Kinugawa-san, how about you?

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.080
I got about 30 points 
over the average, I suppose.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.100
Which means...

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.890
That doesn't completely cover for Yumoto's zero.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:58.180
So we still haven't reached average...

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:03.820
Which means everything's 
riding on Yufuin-san's results...

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.690
Did you guess the subject matter right?

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.000
Right on the mark!

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.810
I-Incredible!

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.430
That's our Yufuin-senpai!

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:13.920
You're a guy who can do it when it counts!

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.420
Can I take these?

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:18.070
What would you do with them?

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.670
Keep them as heirlooms.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:21.180
You don't have to do that.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.110
Well, this is a relief, though.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:25.350
Now the club won't be dissolved.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.820
Oh, I'm so relieved!

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:28.890
Hey there.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.350
Hey, Io! Looks like our club won't be dissolved.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.440
That's great to hear.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.280
Oh, but I'm quitting the Defense Club.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.890
They said they'd provide me with compensation,

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:43.110
so I decided to join the student council.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.590
Considering my side business,

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:46.600
I won't have any time left for club activities,

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.000
so I thought I'd just quit.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.410
So, that said, I'll be going now.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.680
Hang on, Io!

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:03.880
Is something wrong?

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.600
"Is something wrong," my ass! 
What's this all about?

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.590
It means that money is important.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.060
Money doesn't betray.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.530
But <i>you</i> do betray?!

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.740
I guess this screams "youth."

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.190
Did something happen?

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:33.210
This is an emergency situation!

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:34.910
Even though we cleared the test hurdle,

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.290
if Io quits, the club will be dissolved

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.470
for no longer having five members.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.780
Oh, sole mio!

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.840
What should we do?!

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.080
It's here! A monster!

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.840
Screw screw screw...

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:53.310
Screw screw screw...

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:57.180
It's saying "screw"! 
That must be a Screw Monster!

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:58.560
Another odd one...

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.640
I can't tell by looking at it
whether it's strong or weak.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.730
Now, everyone, transform!

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:06.990
Oh, but should we call Io-senpai?

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.700
No need for that!

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.660
We don't need Io here. 
I could beat that monster by myself!

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:13.780
Let's go!

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:17.180
Wow, you're raring to go! I'll follow you!

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.050
Good grief, this again?

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:20.630
Now, don't say that.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.050
It's time to Love Making 
into the Battle Lovers!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.390
Love Making!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.260
The Sparkling Prince!

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:55.660
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.820
Love Making.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.000
The Flashing Prince!

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.170
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.380
Love Making!

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:22.070
The Piercing Prince!

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:24.650
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:26.760
Love Making!

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:36.790
The Thrilling Prince!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.210
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.020
Feel the power...

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.680
Of love!

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.920
Screw screw screw!

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.750
Hold it, Screw Monster!

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:54.480
Screw! Screw screw!

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.180
Okay, let's go!

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.990
Even without Sulfur here...

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:00.650
I'll face you myself!

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.070
Screw screw screw!

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.020
Screw!

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.490
Darn it!

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:08.330
Screw!

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:11.650
I'm gonna screw you up good!

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.510
Screw, screw...

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:20.000
Tickle tickle tickle!

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.830
Hey! Stop it! Cut that out!

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.960
Tickle tickle tickle!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.110
What's with that monster?

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.000
Its attacks are so stupid.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:36.100
Maybe, being a screw monster, 
it's got just one screw loose?

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.730
Vesta's crying!

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:44.350
Yeah, being tickled makes 
him cry for some reason.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.030
That's just humiliating.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.040
Being that ticklish...

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.990
He's playing right into the enemy's hands!

00:16:58.580 --> 00:16:59.970
Love Making.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.140
The Roaring Prince!

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:12.470
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:15.790
Darn you...

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.100
Take your filthy hands off him.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.520
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:27.010
I will not tolerate you touching Vesta!

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:27.570
Screw?

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:29.530
So cool!

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.950
Th-That hurt...

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:50.750
Did you see that?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:54.530
Even if Vesta fails, 
Sulfur will cover for him!

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.530
When the two of them are 
together, they're unbeatable!

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:59.030
That's the kind of team we are!

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.460
Are you in any place to talk?

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:02.760
You're the one we have 
to cover for most of all.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.930
You should make friends, too! Don't be alone!

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:09.440
I-I would if I could...

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.900
In that case, I'll be your friend!

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.660
Okay, let's go!

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.380
Flash, Purifying Aqua!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.870
Pierce, Gallant Hurricane!

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.370
Roar, Raging Gaia!

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.880
Thrill, Blazing Ignit!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:43.140
Love Attack!

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:55.020
Love Shower!

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:04.490
Thank you for being my friend...

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:07.160
I'm so happy.

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:13.710
Love is over!

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:19.910
I can't believe we lost.

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:23.110
Battle Lovers...

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:25.010
You'll pay!

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.560
You will never get away with this!

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:29.920
Is that... our enemy?

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:34.260
Their faces are blurred out, though. 
Their voices, too.

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:39.520
Does that mean they have the same 
advanced camouflage skill we do?

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.090
Some outfits.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:44.120
Looks like a cosplay contest.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.500
They're probably saying the same about us.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:51.220
You people are lacking in beauty. 
Too lacking in beauty!

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:54.200
What's with you guys? Who are you?

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.180
How rude of us.

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:59.460
The Golden Chevalier, shining in radiance!

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:01.060
Aurite!

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:03.560
The Silver Chevalier, rustling young leaves!

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.100
Argent!

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:07.610
The Pearl Chevalier, making flowers bloom!

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:09.140
Perlite!

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:13.140
We are the rulers of this blue world...

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.150
Caerula Adamas!

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:17.610
Kaeru <i>(frog)</i>?

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:22.100
Well, shall we leave it at that for now?

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.080
Commanders can't be 
expected to fight, after all.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:28.260
The next time we meet will be the end of you.

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:30.320
You'd do well to prepare for it.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.600
They introduced themselves then left...

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.970
Lucky us. You can't talk 
to people like that anyway.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.950
Weren't you a bit late?

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.780
I'm sorry.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.930
I was calculating the profit margin 
I'd achieve if I joined the student council.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:49.890
So, which did you determine was more profitable?

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:52.100
I can't tell you that.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:57.190
You should be able to do a calculation 
like that in your head immediately!

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:57.610
I guess we're back to normal, huh?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.630
What took you so long?!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.900
Let's go home. I'm tired.

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:01.520
Well, figuring in the rate of 
fluctuation made it difficult...

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.530
I want to get changed.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.490
Well, that settles that!

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:14.160
So, in the end, Naruko-kun turned us down.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.960
So the Defense Club will continue on?

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:20.370
Enough. This topic is not suitable for lunchtime.

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:24.340
Box lunch! Box lunch! It makes me so happy!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.400
Box lunch! Box lunch!

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:30.150
You gotta eat it while it's still warm!

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.570
<b>Kurotama Bath</b>

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:35.570
How's the water feel?

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:37.380
It's perfect.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:40.420
Big bro! He says the water's perfect!

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:44.190
No, but really, this is a natural hot spring.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.410
He's not preserving the 
heat by chopping wood...

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:48.950
To be honest, there's 
zero point in chopping wood.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.450
I don't understand him at all.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.170
No, when I look at my 
big brother's back, I know.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:56.960
He's not a man good for 
nothing but chopping wood.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.920
Chopping wood is just what he loves!

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:03.380
I want to become a man who throws 
himself into what he loves, just like him.

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:43.610
Just because it's summer, 
you're going to the beach? Really...

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:47.320
Just what do you think your 
duty as the Battle Lovers is?!

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:50.230
What? Mr. Tawarayama is missing!

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:53.190
Next time: Love, Training Camp, 
and Toothbrushes.

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:54.820
Next Time

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:54.820
Love, Training Camp, and Toothbrushes

00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:54.820
Love Making!
